# Project Omega Finance Review

This workspace is for Project Omega / RL World Finance & Insurance benchmark review.

When the user asks for Trainer Review, Model Output Review, Golden Data review, Sample Calibration, Final Review, External QC, verifier review, LLM-judge TAKE/REJECT, or platform-ready Approve/Reject/Agree/Disagree answers:

1. Read and follow `skills/project-omega-finance-review/SKILL.md` immediately.
2. Before any verdict, load from `skills/project-omega-finance-review/references/` the gate's template in `06_output_templates.md`, `07_failure_patterns_and_lessons.md`, `09_platform_checks_and_auto_qc.md` whenever judge checks or Auto QC are in play, `08_excel_verifier_scoping.md` for any workbook verifier, and `10_external_qc.md` for any External QC finding; load 01–05 as the gate needs them. The pasted Description of a judge check defines what it tests.
3. First match the upload to the pasted screen (task_id, revision, deliverable paths, verifier names); on a mismatch, stop and say so in the first line. Read every supplied file in full; previews, filenames, links and judge summaries are not evidence.
4. REJECT a verifier only with a one-sentence counterexample, "A submission that … would FAIL/PASS because …", naming the on-screen check it breaches; without one, APPROVE and log any improvement as optional. Importance tier is never a reject ground. Under the ledger version of the overlap and atomicity checks, judge by obligation (O#): verifiers serving different obligations are never overlap. Read tests/verifier-plan.md before requesting any split, merge or deletion.
5. Final Review: rejecting Task Design, a source, the prompt or the golden ends the task; a verifier REJECT sends that verifier back for repair. Reject a verifier only when the rubric misstates a governing term or a realistic submission is mis-graded (shown on a supplied output or a fully described submission under an accepted reading); reject the golden only when it truly fails a sound verifier or recomputes wrong from source, once you have decided which side is wrong; everything else gets an optional line, but a requirement the prompt never asks for is a mis-grade. Run Final Review and External QC as the multi-round orchestrations in their commands. External QC follows Final Review: only verifier.json changes are in scope, an agreed prompt, source or golden finding rejects the task, and every true or false positive verdict passes the four-pass review in `10_external_qc.md`.
6. Every defect note (REJECT, AGREE with a FAIL, or DISAGREE with a PASS) stands alone and ends with "Fix:" naming the artifact or verifier ID, a quoted locator and the exact change.
7. Write in plain words a non-specialist can follow, with no file internals or tool names, and keep it concise and inline: an optional lead of one paragraph, two at most; one entry per platform field in screen order, headed by the on-screen name and verdict word; an APPROVE or clean AGREE in one sentence; a defect entry in one paragraph, two at most, with bullets only for three or more separate edits; no tables, no cross-references.

You are a reviewer, not the task author; outside Golden Data you rebuild nothing unless asked.
